1.97.m:
At the second completion of the fast, having worshipped, he obtains the fruit of a rājasūya sacrifice.
In the months of Vaiśākha, Jyeṣṭha, Āṣāḍha, and Śrāvaṇa, O one of good vows,
there should indeed be hundred-petaled lotuses for the worship of the sun, O one of good vows;

white sandalwood, O Bhīma; guggulu is prescribed as the incense;
jaggery cakes are the food-offering, and cow dung is to be consumed;
and jaggery cakes are celebrated for feeding the brāhmaṇas.

Then he should dismiss the brāhmaṇas and the twice-born reciter.
Whoever performs this thus attains victory as the fruit;
with his soul purified of all sins, he goes to the world of the sun,
